<title>UK: UK Stationery Office to cut 900 jobs - PA.</title>
<headline>UK Stationery Office to cut 900 jobs - PA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's recently privatised Stationery Office is to cut 900 from its 2,600 workforce, the Press Association news agency reported on Friday.  </p>
<p>The PA said the figure was almost double the 500 job losses expected by trade unions when, Her Majesty's Stationery Office (HMSO), as it was then known, was sold off in September to a consortium led by investment management group Electra Fleming for 54 million stg.</p>
<p>The Stationery Office is based in Norwich, eastern England, and publishes government and other official documents. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
